==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la}}, from {{etyl|grc}} {{term|lang=grc|ἀρθρῖτις|tr=arthritis||joint-disease, gout}}, from {{term|ἄρθρον|lang=grc|tr=arthron||a joint}}. See also [[arthro-]] and [[-itis]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ɑː(ɹ)θˈɹaɪtɪs/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|pl=arthritides}}

# [[inflammation|Inflammation]] of a [[joint]] or joints causing [[pain]] and/or [[disability]], swelling and stiffness, and due to various causes such as [[infection]], [[trauma]], degenerative changes or [[metabolic]] disorders.

====Derived terms====
* [[arthritic]]
* [[arthritically]]
* [[osteoarthritis]]
* [[polyarthritis]]
* [[rheumatoid arthritis]]

